#: ../../source/readme_rosetta.rst:24
msgid "readme_rosetta.markdown_handler module"
msgstr ""
"README\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"### `rosetta.markdown_handler`\n"
"\n"
"Handle markdown in a readable and extensible way.\n"
"\n"
"### Features\n"
"\n"
"*   **Readability**\n"
"    *   Provides a simple interface for rendering Markdown text.\n"
"    *   Used throughout the app to make content more readable.\n"
"*   **Flexibility**\n"
"    *   Allows you to easily customize the styling of your README file.\n"
"    *   Supports HTML and CSS files for custom styling.\n"
"\n"
"### Usage\n"
"\n"
"1.  Import `markdown_handler` in your app:\n"
"    ```python\n"
"from rosetta.markdown_handler import markdown_handler\n"
"```\n"
"2.  Use it on any Markdown text:\n"
"    ```python\n"
"markdown_text = \"This is a [test link](https://www.example.com).\"\n"
"rendered_markdown = markdown_handler.render(markdown_text)\n"
"print(rendered_markdown)  # Output: This is a <a href=\"https://www.example.com\">test link</a>.\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"### Customization\n"
"\n"
"*   **HTML and CSS Files**\n"
"    *   To customize the styling of your README file, create an HTML file named `index.html` in your repository root.\n"
"    *   The HTML should include any necessary stylesheets or scripts you want to use.\n"
"\n"
"*   **CSS File Naming Conventions**\n"
"    *   When creating a custom CSS file, follow this naming convention: `<name>.css`.\n"
"    *   For example, if the name of your README file is `README.md`, create an HTML file named `index.html` and a CSS file named `readme.css`.\n"
"\n"
"*   **Customizing the Readme Handler**\n"
"    *   To customize the behavior of the `markdown_handler`, you can extend it by creating a new class.\n"
"    *   Make sure to import your custom handler in your app, then use it in place of the original."

